# Local 9router client

The official hub skill is installed at `~/.agents/skills/9router/SKILL.md` and
links to capability instructions for chat, embeddings and other endpoints.

Private settings are in `~/.config/9router/client.env`:

- `NINEROUTER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:20128` (no trailing `/v1`).
- `NINEROUTER_KEY` is the user-authorized active local API credential. Read it only
  inside a requesting process; never print it, put it in command arguments, or
  retain it in repository or memory documents.

Use `${NINEROUTER_URL}/v1/...` with the Bearer credential. The selected Hindsight
models remain `qwen-combo` and `qwen3-chat/qwen3-embeddings`. Authenticated health
and model discovery pass; the same key is already configured for Hindsight.

`verification.json` records configuration checks. `inference-check.json` records
bounded synthetic probes, which exposed an intermittent chat 503 and an embedding
timeout. Do not mistake discovery/authentication success for healthy inference.
Do not silently change models, disable authentication or alter approval settings.

## Swap-aware startup

Use `~/.local/bin/9router-local --tray --skip-update`; login autostart already
uses this launcher. It loads `~/.config/9router/runtime.env`, setting fetch,
first-chunk and stall deadlines to 600 seconds before starting the installed
CLI. The package and provider credentials are unchanged. Direct bare `9router`
launches do not load these overrides unless the environment is already set.

The earlier `inference-check.json` is historical. Current swap diagnosis,
queue limits and rollback guidance live in `~/.config/hindsight/README.md`;
current validation is in `~/.local/state/hindsight/swap-reliability-verification.json`.
